  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between 7,2',6'-Trihydroxy-5-methoxyflavanone and SCCH-26 through a series of target interactions. This compound appears to act as a target for SNU-387, which in turn is a target of Tetraethylammonium and Npc13565, all of which ultimately target SCCH-26. The consistent presence of these intermediaries indicates a possible pathway where 7,2',6'-Trihydroxy-5-methoxyflavanone may influence SCCH-26 through these molecular intermediates. The evidence suggests a possible mechanism involving the modulation of signaling pathways or receptor activation, though the exact nature of the interaction remains unclear. The integration of these targets highlights the compound's potential role in modulating cellular processes linked to SCCH-26, though further experimental validation is needed to confirm the precise mechanism.",
